@startuml
title US10 - Register a Test Type\nSequence Diagram (SD) - Default Successful Flow

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Administrator" as User
participant "view:RegisterTestTypeView" as View
participant "controller:RegisterTestTypeController" as Ctrl
participant "App (static access)" as App
participant "app:App" as AppInstance
participant "container:TestTypeContainer" as Container

User -> View : requests Test Type registration
activate View
View --> User : requests Internal Code, NHS Code,\nand collection-method description
User -> View : provides the requested data
View -> Ctrl : registerTestType(internalCode, nhsCode,\ncollectionMethodDescription)
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> App : getInstance()
App --> Ctrl : app
Ctrl -> AppInstance : getTestTypeContainer()
AppInstance --> Ctrl : container
Ctrl -> Container : create(internalCode, nhsCode,\ncollectionMethodDescription)
activate Container
create participant "testType:TestType" as TestType
Container -> TestType : TestType(internalCode, nhsCode,\ncollectionMethodDescription)
activate TestType
TestType -> TestType : isValidInternalCode(internalCode)
TestType -> TestType : isValidNhsCode(nhsCode)
TestType --> Container : constructed TestType
deactivate TestType
Container --> Ctrl : testType
deactivate Container
Ctrl -> Container : save(testType)
activate Container
Container -> Container : existsByInternalCode(internalCode)
Container -> Container : existsByNhsCode(nhsCode)\n(case-insensitive)
note right of Container
Both identities are unused in this success flow.
end note
Container -> Container : append testType to testTypes
Container --> Ctrl : true
deactivate Container
Ctrl --> View : true
deactivate Ctrl
View --> User : confirms registration success
deactivate View

@enduml
